ks f2 and h2 pawns horizontally. Could be useful, but Qxb1 is immediate material gain.  \n\nAlso note Black’s queen on d8 is still unmoved (F0), so maybe keep it safe. Qa1 is the promoted queen, can be used aggressively.  \n\nReason: Qxb1 captures a rook for nothing, increases material advantage decisively. It also possibly opens lines for other pieces. There’s no downside as queen is not endangered (no White piece attacks a1). So it’s a straightforward winning move.  \n\nAnswer: Q: a1-b1'}
