apture? White king at e2 is far, safe.  \n  3. **K: c6-d6** – centralize king to support pawns in the center/king side.  \n  4. **P: a7-a5** or **a7-a6** – start advancing the a-pawn.  \n\nReason: The safest route is to activate the rook to control the board and restrict the white king, while pushing pawns that cannot be stopped. Since white has no pieces besides the king, any pawn push will eventually lead to a promotion. I choose **R: h1-a1** because it places the rook on the queenside where it can support the a- and b-pawns’ advances and also be ready to cut off the white king from that side. It also avoids any risk of stalemate in the short term.  \n\nAnswer: R: h1-a1'}
