\n1 |    |    |    |    |    |KWF1|    |    | 1\n  +----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+\n     a    b    c    d    e    f    g    h \nYour valid moves are (src-dst-promotion, or src-dst):\n[P: a7-a5, P: a7-a6, P: b2-b1-q, P: b2-b1-n, P: b2-b1-b, P: b2-b1-r, P: b7-b5, P: b7-b6, K: c6-b5, K: c6-b6, K: c6-c5, K: c6-c7, K: c6-d5, K: c6-d6, K: c6-d7, P: f7-f5, P: f7-f6, P: g7-g5, P: g7-g6]\nYour answer format should be: Answer: piece-name: move. \nPiece-name and move (src-dst-promotion or src-dst) should be directly copied EXACTLY from valid move list.\nExample of valid output format: N: a1-b3; P: e7-e8-q; Piece B: g5-f4.\nPlease select a move from your valid moves that maximize your probability of winning.\n', 'reasoning': '', 'output': 'Situation: The board is very sparse with only a few pieces. Black has a king at c6, pawns at a7, b7, f7, g7 (all unmoved), and a pawn at b2 that has moved before (PBF1). White has only a king at f1 (KWF1). Black\'s pawn on b2 is deep in White\'s territory (rank 2), poised to promote. White\'s king is far away on f1. This is a king and pawn endgame where Black has a significant material advantage due to the advanced pawn on b2 and multiple other pawns. Black\'s king is actively placed in the center.\n\nEvaluation:  \n- The pawn on b2 is one step from promotion. Promoting to a queen is overwhelmingly strong, giving a decisive material advantage.  \n- The white king is on f1, far from the b2 pawn. It cannot catch the pawn if we promote immediately.  \n- Other moves like moving the a7 or f7 pawns are less urgent and don\'t capitalize on the immediate winning opportunity.  \n- Moving the king might help, but promoting the pawn is the fastest route to checkmate.\n\nReason: The most forcing and winning move is to promote the b2 pawn to a queen. Promotion to a queen is strongest, giving immediate overwhelming material. Promotion to other pieces (knight, rook, bishop) would still leave a piece advantage but delay checkmate. Given White has only a king, a queen ensures quick checkmate. The move "P: b2-b1-q" is directly winning and the most efficient.\n\nAnswer: P: b2-b1-q'}
