4 looks strong. Also Kc6-d5 centralizes.\n\nBut maybe pushing pawns is good too: f7-f5 opens possibility for f5-f4 etc., but not urgent.\n\nI\'ll choose Qb1-e4 as it improves queen position most.\n\nReason: Qe4 places queen in center, controlling many squares, ready to coordinate with king to chase White king. It avoids stalemate (leaves king legal moves) and keeps flexibility for pawn pushes or checkmating net.\n\nAnswer: Q: b1-e4'}
