ant, White king could check and harass queen; better to have king nearer.  \n2. **K: c5-d5** – Centralize king toward both queenside and kingside pawns, preparing to support b2 promotion more safely next turn.  \n3. **P: f7-f5** – Opens path for f-pawn, gains space, maybe distract White king.  \n4. **P: a4-a3** – Advances a-pawn, but b2 promotion is faster win.  \n\n**Reason:**  \nThe fastest win is to queen a pawn while ensuring White king can’t immediately capture it or perpetually check. b2→b1 is one move from queening, but after promotion, queen on b1 is far from our king (c5). White king at g4 is 5 squares away (distance = |g4-b1| = 5 files and 3 ranks → about 6 king moves away). So White king can’t reach b1 next turn; queen is safe immediately after promotion. Once we have queen, checkmate with king+queen vs. lone king is trivial. So promoting now is perfectly safe and accelerates win. Therefore **P: b2-b1-q** is best.\n\n**Answer:** P: b2-b1-q'}
