 strong central square that controls many key squares (e4, e5, d4, d6, etc.) and puts maximum pressure on White’s position without risk of immediate stalemate. It’s more active than moving sideways or backward and keeps the option to approach White King gradually.  \n\n**Answer:** K: c4-d5'}
